From b9ef866571fdbc2281aa3d4c03244599e7f5bc59 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 02:44:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] feat(yocv): connected journey cards, YoID thread and the
 link back to Ziqi
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Journey contract v1, Phase 4. SkillLens opens YoCV with ?as=halima and
journey=demo plus the contract params (from, yoid, listing, goal, plan,
course, credential, return).

- core.js: journeyParams reads the nine params only when journey=demo,
  trimmed and length-capped. journeyReturn follows only an absolute
  http(s) return. journeyBackHref builds <return>?journey=demo&from=yocv
  &yoid=...&application=app-001, with & when the return has a query and
  before any fragment. journeyThread gives each step its state.
- yoid.js: the params leave the address as ?as= does and stay in
  sessionStorage (yocv.journey) for the tab, so hash routes and a reload
  keep them. Arriving on no route opens #/cv, where the card is.
- app.js: in journey mode and online, the arriving card (From SkillLens
  · Phase 3, Skill Credential) tops Step 1, the YoID thread tops every
  step, and after Apply the leaving card (Back to Ziqi · Phase 1, Job
  Application) links back to the listing in the same tab. No http(s)
  return: the card shows without the button.
- data/journey.json: a connected block with the phase, the thread names
  and the two cards' items. The existing keys are unchanged.
- cv-copy.js: the card and thread copy, word for word from the contract.
- styles.css: the card and the strip in the contract colours; --blue
  (#4cade9) joins the tokens. The button text is ink: white on that blue
  reads at 2.6:1.

Without journey=demo nothing changes: no card, no strip, no extra key.
cred-002 kept its "Skill Credential, from SkillLens" tag either way.

House tests changed on purpose: restyle.test.cjs lists the new --blue
token; yoid-shell.test.cjs now allows the journey key beside the person
key in sessionStorage.

npm test (YOCV_LIVE_YOMA=0, Node 22): tests 671, pass 639, fail 0,
skipped 4, cancelled 28 (the provider timeout tests, as on main here).

